From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: inthewaves <inthewaves@pm.me>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 18:06:37 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [bugfix] Avoid resetting IME state on window focus loss

Window focus can move to a popup while the underlying text field remains focused. The
unconditional reset added by upstream d411ccf133376a271e736e1dd9892f9a8833ac6d clears the editor
state and hides the keyboard in this case. Opening the spelling suggestion popup reproduces this.

Remove only the reset on window focus loss. Keep the renderer state refresh on window focus gain
and the existing cleanup on view or activity focus loss. Android already restarts input when the
window regains focus without an active input connection.
---
 .../src/org/chromium/content/browser/input/ImeAdapterImpl.java   | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/content/public/android/java/src/org/chromium/content/browser/input/ImeAdapterImpl.java b/content/public/android/java/src/org/chromium/content/browser/input/ImeAdapterImpl.java
index b74a52b4347bc..ca3435c6a8a12 100644
--- a/content/public/android/java/src/org/chromium/content/browser/input/ImeAdapterImpl.java
+++ b/content/public/android/java/src/org/chromium/content/browser/input/ImeAdapterImpl.java
@@ -1028,7 +1028,6 @@ public class ImeAdapterImpl
     public void onWindowFocusChanged(boolean gainFocus) {
         if (DEBUG_LOGS) Log.i(TAG, "onWindowFocusChanged: gainFocus [%b]", gainFocus);
 
-        if (!gainFocus) resetAndHideKeyboard();
         if (gainFocus
                 && isValid()
                 && ContentFeatureMap.isEnabled(
